    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After the NEET-UG exam on May 3, 2026, a courageous whistleblower delivered ironclad proof of the paper leak directly to authorities. Four days later, the evidence prompted India's National Testing Agency to act decisively, handing the entire matter to the Central Bureau of Investigation. This swift response led to the arrest of thirteen individuals, including a trainer linked to the scandal. In a stand for justice, the compromised exam was annulled to protect fairness, and a new date was set for June 21 to ensure students receive a proper chance.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Hero",
        "fragments": [
